WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.870
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.700
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.750
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.080
"A giant robot suddenly appears"
"What exactly is Hizakuriger?"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.410
"And what is waiting for them on Mars?"
"Truth Found From an Octopus"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.950
"And what is waiting for them on Mars?"
"Truth Found From an Octopus"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪
  

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:56.750
Hizakuriger!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.410
They combined?!

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.370
Turning into a robot is fine and all,
but now what do we do, lower half?

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.370
Don't call me lower half, upper half.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.660
Heh, if you're the lower half,
you'll listen to what the upper half tells you.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.120
Hey, you couldn't tell me what to do
in a billion years, upper half.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.620
Well, look who's getting into a tizzy
despite being the lower half.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.870
I told you to shut up! The upper half
couldn't exist without the lower half!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.330
You nitwit, the lower half couldn't
exist without the upper half!

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.660
The brain is up on my end, after all.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.200
Well, you couldn't even stand up
without the lower half!

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.330
Yeah, without the lower half,
I couldn't pee standing up, huh?

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.580
Shut up! Don't make fun of the lower half!

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.700
Oh, so you admit you're the lower half!

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.910
Shut up, upper half!

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.950
Whatever, just hurry it up, lower half.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.200
--Don't tell me what to do, upper half!

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.080
--Hey, you guys! It doesn't matter
if you're upper half or lower half!
--Don't tell me what to do, upper half!

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.040
Hurry up and shut down the tractor beam!

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.910
Yeah, and we were just
about to do something!

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.080
Oh, is this it?

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.120
Huh?

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.830
Bingo! Nicely done, lower half!

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.620
I said don't call me lower half!

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.620
Mr. Yang, 

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.910
the robot is about to fire
an awesome-looking weapon!

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.540
It looks bad, Mr. Yang!

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.120
Emergency retreat!

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.000
It's no use! We won't make it!

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.540
Go!

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.660
Huh?

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.910
Huh? It just lit up?

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.580
What's going on?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.370
What are you waiting for?! We gotta run!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.290
Run?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.370
We're gonna warp! Hurry back to the ship!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.290
Getting back might be asking a lot.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.950
Just grab hold as-is, upper half! 

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.950
Huh? Don't tell me what to do!

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.250
The upper half is the only one
that can grab on! Move it, upper half!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.330
How dare you talk to me like that!
You're just a lower half!

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.660
What did you say, upper half?!

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.870
Look, just grab on, right now!

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.080
Mr. Yang!

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.330
They're trying to get away!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.120
Aw, shoot them! Shoot them!

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.950
Whoa, now they're firing at us!

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.160
Heading to warp now!

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.660
Fantastic!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.580
Mr. Yang!

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.790
The robot disappeared with the spaceship.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.660
Then start chasing them, right now!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.290
But we don't know where they're going.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:39.700
Hmph, how many humans and aliens
do you think I've chased in my time?

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.830
I've got a good idea what goes on up here
with those who run from collectors.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.330
It's said that criminals in Japan
once fled to the north.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.500
That was no doubt because they thought 

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.700
Hokkaido was the most distant
place they could reach.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.200
However, things are different now. 

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.660
The "distant place" is the ends of the universe.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.540
--"The ends of the universe"?
--"The ends of the universe"?

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.750
In other words, the off ramp of the Milky Way

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.370
where the Galaxy Highway has
its Checkpoint No. 1--Haccone.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.750
--Mr. Yang, you're amazing!
--Mr. Yang, you're amazing!

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.000
Remember, don't let go,
no matter what, Robby.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.660
That's "Mr. Robby" to you, you little twerp!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.290
Okay, don't let go,
no matter what, Mr. Upper Half.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.500
Don't call me Mr. That!

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.080
Ah, that was interesting!

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.330
I'm impressed you made it back. Kudos.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.410
Huh? Who do you think you are?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.830
By the way, what is the deal
with this spaceship?

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.200
Oh, it's my old man's.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.410
When I ran away from home,
I took it from our shed.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:54.160
Then I set down on that building's roof
while it was under construction

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.410
and made it into my residence.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.080
Oh, yeah?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.040
So, that Hizakuriger robot, too?

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.620
I know nothing about that.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.790
What's wrong, Ikku?

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.250
Out of fuel. We're warping out.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.750
What? I thought we were going straight
to Checkpoint No. 1 at Haccone.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.410
Quit your griping.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.290
Head for Haccone!

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.160
--Yes, sir!
--Yes, sir!

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.040
Where are we?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.500
Fourth planet of the solar system, Mars.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.250
Mars?! We're right next to Earth, aren't we?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:34.200
Nothing I can do about it. We're out of gas.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.910
Awesome! We're here!
We really are here on Mars!

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:46.290
Yeah, good on you. And now,
you're going to get out.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.290
--Huh?
--This is goodbye. Adios.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.120
That can't be the case. 

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:54.200
--Huh?
--You have to pay back that money.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:58.450
I told you, once I get to Isekandar and
become a millionaire, I'll give it back.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.370
Then I'm sticking with you until then.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.700
I'm gonna pay your boss back directly,
so get the hell out.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.080
Hey, once he's off the ship,
we're gonna keep on going.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.500
I told you, we're out of gas, lamebrain.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.790
Besides, you should have it properly serviced. 

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.830
This ship hasn't flown
in over a dozen years, right?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.540
Do you really think we can
get it serviced on Mars?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:24.000
Mars is a place filled with
octopuses who have floppy limbs.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:29.410
What year are you living in? 

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:33.540
Those Martians are a work of fiction
H. G. Wells wrote about long ago.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.290
Oh, no, I've seen them on the web.
They're definitely octopuses.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.790
--It's fiction!
--They're octopuses!

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.950
--They are not!
--They're octopuses, I'm telling you! 

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.080
--Octopuses! Octopuses! Octopuses!
--Are not! Are not! Are not!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.330
Stop it! Shut the hell up!

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.750
Welcome!

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.410
Fill it up with regular.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:53.660
Right. Can I clean your windshield?
Offer you a wash?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.790
The windshield, please. Don't need a wash.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.120
Very well.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.750
There, you see? An octopus, right?

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.700
Sir, what kind of service would you like?

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.080
You offer service?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.540
Of course! But I can't say how much
it will cost without having a look first.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.200
That's fine. He'll be paying for it.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.370
--Huh?
--Thank you!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.330
Why do I have to put up the service costs, too?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:27.410
Because I gave you a lift from
Earth to Mars. Consider it your fare.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:30.120
As someone who's in debt, you're the
last one I need to hear that from.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.120
You've got an answer for everything. 

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.450
Go ahead back to Earth or Isekandar
all on your own, you little brat.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.200
If that's how it is, I won't
pay for your service costs.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.580
Huh? Now look here...!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.870
Sirs, we're here.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.370
That will be 720 mons. 

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.790
Wow! Look at this! There's
nothing but Martians here!

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.450
Dude, why are you having so much fun
looking at octopus people?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.870
Hey, want to try some of that?

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:00.450
Huh? The takoyaki stand?
What are they, cannibals?

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:04.370
Takoyaki made by Martians!
Come on, it's my treat!

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.750
Who do you think you are?!

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.160
Here you go.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.870
Thank you.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.080
Here, dig in.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.790
Thank you. Wait, you don't tell me to dig in!

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.000
Whoever has the money
in life gets the final say.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:26.370
How lame! Can't take the heat, you wussy?

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.200
Whoo, that was hot. But still good.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.660
Come to think of it, takoyaki has
flour in it. Are you okay with that?

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:38.000
I figured you'd say something about
going gluten-free being better.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.620
You don't get it, do you? 

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:40.620
Huh?

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:45.330
This isn't just any takoyaki;
this is takoyaki made by Martians.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.450
Plus, it's 4.8 stars.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.120
"4.8 stars"?

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.250
I-It's nothing. 

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.200
You know, this is just regular takoyaki.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.870
What would you do if this octopus
came from one of those Martians?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:58.700
Huh?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.330
Say there's a Martian prison
out in that desert where we were,

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.290
and this octopus came from one of their legs.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.500
This came... from a Martian's... legs?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.830
That would be so awesome!

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:14.870
Mister! Another order, please!

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.830
Is he for real?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.830
Mr. Yang, we'll reach
Planet Haccone very shortly.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.410
"Haccone"
Mr. Yang, Haccone is supposed
to be famous for its hot springs.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.160
Hot springs, eh? 

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.620
As long as we're here, why don't we
stop in at the hot springs for a dip?

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.450
--Hooray!
--Hooray!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:40.250
Hmm, Robby, before I have you,
I'm going to wash my body off.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:47.870
These octopus crackers are good.
They're just ordinary octopuses.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.580
Well of course they are.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.290
Want one?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.750
No thanks. 

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.330
And you need to find a ship to take you
home after you finish eating that.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:58.200
Hey, sailor! Hey, sailor!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.500
Hey, sailor! Hey, sailor! You from Earth?

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.290
Sailor? You mean me?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.660
Yes, you, sailor. 

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:09.870
Ooh, damn, you're glamorous!
Mm-hmm, I did, I did! I came from Earth!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.120
Listen, care to stop by my bar? 

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.000
I do! I do! Let's go!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.950
Huh? H-Hey!

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:20.540
You can come, too! As a last sendoff,
I'll show you how the big boys play.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.410
For the love of...

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.700
Here's to you Martian beauties! 

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.660
Cheers!

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.370
My, sailor, you sure can down a drink!

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:38.000
He's no sailor, he's a debtor. 

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.950
I heard about you.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.200
You and the sailor are making
a pilgrimage to Isekandar together?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.750
Huh? W-Well, yeah...

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.870
Oh, no, no.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.870
He's going bye-bye here. 

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.080
I want to go to Isekandar, too.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.750
So Isekandar is well-known on Mars, too.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:59.000
Of course it is. They play that
commercial around the clock here, too.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.120
Want something to drink?

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.540
Oh, I'm still underage, so...

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.250
Gentleman, gentlemen,
thank you for waiting. 

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.290
The Martian Cabaret,
Cabaret Club's special attraction,

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:11.250
the soft, soft-bodied octo-octo show,
featuring Martian beauties,

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.370
is about to get started!

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:15.330
Yeah! I've been waiting for this!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:18.700
--I'll be in the restroom.
--Yeah, go! Whoo! Whoo!

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.750
Good grief, I can't stand being with him.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.750
Ooh, am I beat.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.660
Me, too.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:36.080
It's so hot.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.750
Seriously. I can't take these suits
for more than an hour.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.620
Th-They're...

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:59.080
Hey, Hatchi, are you enjoying this, too?

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:02.040
Huh? He's gone.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.620
Hey, Hatchi, you in here?

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:06.540
Guess not.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.200
Damn it, who's gonna pay my tab?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.250
Ah, there you are!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.370
I was wondering where you ran off to, sailor.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.750
Oh, I thought my pal was back here.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:21.790
I'm sure he's gone off with another girl.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.830
After this, we should go
somewhere else, just the two of us.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.910
Me and a glamorous girl,
all by ourselves? Yes! Let's go, let's go!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.120
Hey! Let me out of here!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:36.120
Hey!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.830
"No signal"
  

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.200
"No signal"
It's no use. 

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.700
What kind of situation am I in? 

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.160
It's awesome! Insanely awesome!

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.200
Hey! What's so funny?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.790
I mean, it's funny, right? 

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.160
Here I thought there were
really octopus-people Martians,

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.950
and it turns out they're just
people wearing suits!

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:03.370
On top of that, I'm locked up
out here in the desert!

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:07.080
If I'd lived a normal life,
this would have never happened!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.580
It's insanely awesome!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:12.540
Hey, you're wearing a suit, too, right?

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.080
Y-Yeah.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.290
Isn't it hard to move around in?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:20.370
It's the Earthlings' fault that we have
to wear octopus suits in the first place!

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.620
The Earthlings' fault?

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.540
Mars is the way it is now
because it has been terraformed

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:29.080
thanks to high-level technology, but originally,

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.160
it was an inhospitable world,
full of nothing but deserts,

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:33.540
with an average temperature of -65 degrees.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:38.330
That's why we once wore protective suits,
to allow us to survive.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.080
But then, one day, some Earthlings
arrived here from Earth.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:45.200
Martians! Martians! Martians! Martians!

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:49.040
That news spread around Earth
as though it were the truth.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:53.000
I see. And with the recent
boom in space travel...

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:57.450
So you've built up a tourist planet
geared toward Earthlings?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.830
Yes! Got it!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.830
Sailor, you're amazing!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.410
Here, a present for you.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.950
Thank you. Hey, this time, get me that one.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.330
All righty... let's see...

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:12.540
So, glamorous girl,
what should we do after this?

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.750
The game center is fun and all, 

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.660
but I think a little "interplanetary
exchange" might be good, too.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.660
Oh, yeah! I got it, glamorous girl!

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:22.870
Huh?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:29.000
Glamorous girl?

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.500
Found you!

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.120
A h-h-human glamorous girl?!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:41.330
Shh! If this gets out, there'll be trouble!
They'll seriously send you to prison!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.700
I see. So that's what happened.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.500
It seems I've said a little too much.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.580
Yes?

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.750
Very well. 

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:59.080
Out. There's something we need you to do.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.700
Orders from the head
of the Mars Tourism Bureau.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:05.790
Huh? Your papa is the head
of the Mars Tourism Bureau?

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:06.950
That's right.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:10.750
Then your papa is the one who
turned Mars into a tourist planet?

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:14.620
Yes, along with a major advertising agency.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:18.660
But lately, Earthlings have started
getting tired of coming here.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.660
Earthlings do tend to become
easily tired of things.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.370
Oh, no! It's about to begin!

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.040
What is?

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.000
What brings you to Mars?!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:32.040
Okay, we're coming to you again today
with a live broadcast from Mars!

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:36.200
I'm the head of the Mars Tourism Bureau,
Chu-Chu Takokawaina.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.950
That's my papa.

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.660
Huh? That?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:43.950
This is a live program being broadcast
by the Mars Tourism Bureau.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.750
Papa and the bureau are trying
desperately to make it look

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.750
like Mars is still really popular with it. 

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.250
Are you serious?

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:55.500
Ah, there's a you eating
takoyaki right now! Excuse me!

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.290
Where are you here from?

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:59.120
F-From Earth!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:03.870
--Hmm? It's him!
--Earth, you say? Mars must be the
most popular place among Earthlings.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.000
So, what brings you to Mars?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.410
Why, to visit the wildly popular
"Takotubo Land," of course.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:13.330
I really am enjoying myself.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:16.120
Takotubo Land is a brand-new attraction, 

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:18.750
which is a real popular spot
among you youngsters, isn't it?

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:20.410
Mind if we come with you?

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.450
Why, yes, please, I'd be delighted.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:26.120
Good grief, if you're going to
read cue cards, do a better job!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.620
He's being worked by Papa. 

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:34.370
Takotubo Land is an utterly unpopular
theme park built by the tourism bureau.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:37.950
The whole planet is one big fictitious sham.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:45.080
We're going to have to go on
living our whole lives as a lie.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.540
Then there's no choice
but to unmask the octopus.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.450
Huh?

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:52.870
The lie that those octopus suits represent!

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.540
Wow. Amazing.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:18:00.870
There are so many octopus pots.
What a marvelous sight.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.660
I'm so glad I came.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.410
Hey! You're not the only one
who gets to be on TV!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.370
Hizakuriger?!

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:18.580
What's that robot doing here?
This isn't in the script!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.250
Hatchi, what are you doing?!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:27.830
So you were able to pilot Hizakuriger
without having both of us.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.790
That doesn't make any difference!
And what is this place, anyway?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.870
There's nothing but octopus pots here!

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:36.000
Is this place really fun?

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.500
Well, they told me to say it's fun.

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:41.500
H-Hey! Stop him! Arrest him immediately!

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:44.250
Papa! Stop it, already!

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:49.750
We Martians aren't octopuses!
This is what we really look like!

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:55.790
Stop! Martians are octopuses!
That's Mars's selling point!

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.620
What other selling point does Mars
have besides being octopuses?!

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:03.040
Papa, we have to stop
putting up this false image.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:06.950
Don't be ridiculous! If this ever
gets out, there will be hell to pay!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.410
It's already gotten out.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.790
This is being broadcast on live TV.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:15.450
Eep! Why are you still shooting?!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.540
It's hopeless. It's all over.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:28.200
Look, trying to paper over the truth by
putting on an act as someone you're not

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.120
is going to bring you nothing but grief.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:36.290
Mars has lots of other selling points
without having to resort to these tricks.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:40.080
Like that daughter of yours.
The real-life article is far more attractive

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:43.000
than the one wearing a strange octopus suit.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.700
Aww...

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.950
S-Still, 

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.000
if we give up being octopuses,
we'll lose our Martian-ness!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.450
That's all right. Just be yourself.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:58.040
Just be... myself...

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.950
Show people who you really are.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:04.120
Show people who I really am...

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.830
Be who you really are.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.160
Be who I really am...

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:12.750
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.790
There's nothing to be afraid of...

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.540
I don't feel cold at all.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.040
Yeah, terrific, terrific!

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:32.330
Being yourself really is the best! I'm amazing!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.080
Keep blowing your own horn.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.000
But do you think they'll be all right?

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:41.660
Hey, I say let beautiful girls be
beautiful girls, and let Mars be Martian.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:44.040
And, hey! Why are you still here, anyway?!

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.750
Why?

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:47.040
Because I want to.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.290
Huh?

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:53.290
Heh, Robby knew he was aboard when
we blasted off. Now he's taking issue?

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:57.620
Besides, who was it that paid the
servicing bill for the ship, again?

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.200
Heh, aw, what the hell.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:03.250
All right, until we get to Isekandar, then.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:09.120
Mr. Yang, we've arrived at Haccone!
Hot springs, hot springs, hot springs!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.160
Wah!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.040
What is it?

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.830
Huge news just hit the web!

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.500
Put it on the main screen!

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.250
"Martians aren't octopuses!"
Martians aren't octopuses?!

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.200
How is that huge news?!

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:23.330
You numbskull! It means Martians
were never octopuses!

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:26.200
No, this is huge news.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.540
Take a look at that photo.

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:34.160
I've found you, Robby.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.290
Men, we're hurrying back to Mars!

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:37.700
--Aw...
--Aw...

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.250
But the hot springs!
The hot springs! The hot springs!

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.870
Be quiet!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:45.200
Robby, I just found something big!

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.330
What? I'm trying to take a shower.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.330
Just come here, quick!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.790
What the hell is it?

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.540
Just take a look at this.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.080
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"
  

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.290
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"
Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger!

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:04.370
♪ With blood boiling hot,
we're off to the galaxy ♪

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:08.540
Wh-What is this? It's an anime
about that robot, isn't it?

00:22:08.540 --> 00:22:11.080
It's a TV anime that was made
a half-century ago,

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:15.830
made in Japan using the classic
"cel" animation method--

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:18.120
Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.910
"A mysterious space patrol stands in the way"
"of the duo as they head for Isekandar"

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:01.910
"What is the wish the
abducted Robby and Hatchi"
"see from the unhappy Plutonians?"
